> we're in the low volume area. That means it's doing nothing other than filling this empty price area with liquidity now. — Source GPS: 4MoNjEQ2Dd8 | [END] | $2,350 in 40 Minutes — Execution mode context: TREND-CONTINUATION and BREAKOUT. Low volume areas are where price moves quickly between volume nodes. — 2.3 Order Flow / Footprint Proof — 2.3.1 Finished Auction = Market Done, Reversal — Definition: A finished auction occurs when one side of the footprint shows zero or near-zero activity. This means the market is done at that price — no more interest. — How it works: — 
> Such a finished auction. So, a completed auction, this gives you the overview that the market was done here. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> Up here, you can see the market had a zero and a nine and 11 and a 20. This means that up here, there was only one side of the price with a number greater than zero. And in such phases, you can simply say there was no more interest here. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> Often, you'll see a zero, a zero, a three, a five, a seven, then you know this auction is really finished. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> And at the top you can simply see that nothing was happening anymore. And we also had a finished auction. That means the market formed a completed auction at the top. — Source GPS: k0zm5NYn0IQ | [BEGINNING] | DAX Crash short — Execution mode context: COUNTER-TRADE. Finished auction at an extreme = reversal signal. — 2.3.2 Unfinished Auction = Continuation — Definition: An unfinished auction occurs when both sides of the footprint show activity. Prices are being accepted. — How it works: — 
> When there are high volumes at the tops or lows, the auctions are very often not yet finished, not yet completed. And only when auctions are completely finished with so-called unfinished auctions, do you have the opportunity to recognize that a sustainable top formation may really be present here. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> There was what is called an unfinished auction here. That means the prices were accepted there. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> up here the market has acceptance. That means the players here are happy and satisfied. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
> if there are so-called unfinished auctions up here at the tops, it gives you the great advantage of recognizing that the market is very likely to keep moving higher. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — Execution mode context: TREND-CONTINUATION. Unfinished auction at a pullback zone = continuation signal. — 2.3.3 Zero on One Side = No Interest — Definition: When the footprint shows zero trades on one side at a price level, there is no counterparty interest. — How it works: — 
> up here, for example, there were zero trades and nine, one level lower at the next price level, there were 11 trades and 20 — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — 
