> You can't control the market. You can only react to the circumstances that arise. — Source GPS: 4MoNjEQ2Dd8 | [END] | $2,350 in 40 Minutes — Context: Price moving in a direction is not proof. You need confirmation at a zone. — 5.2 Volume Alone Is Not Proof — 
> Of course, you also need to use other appropriate filters alongside it. Because it's no use if you just have the cumulative delta somewhere in the middle of the chart. It's just like with other setups. You need to know what you're looking for. — Source GPS: y67l86cSqb8 | [BEGINNING] | CVD Strategy — Context: CVD/delta alone, without a zone and context, is not proof. — 5.3 Extreme Alone Is Not Proof — 
> And even then we have to look into it again. — Source GPS: y67l86cSqb8 | [MIDDLE-END] | CVD Strategy — Context: An extreme reading (volume spike, delta extreme) alone is not enough. Further verification required. — 5.4 First Impulse Is Not Proof — 
> Early short has high stop-out probability — Source GPS: tS6ZEiHj8gQ | [BEGINNING] | Perfect Short Trade — Context: Entering on the first move without waiting for confirmation (fallback below key levels, consolidation) leads to stop-outs. — 5.5 Looks Good Is Not Proof — 
> whenever something looks really, really good, that's when it carries the greatest risks. — Source GPS: tS6ZEiHj8gQ | [BEGINNING] | Perfect Short Trade — Context: When a setup looks perfect, the risk is highest. Proof must be verified, not assumed. — 5.6 Pre-Market Numbers Are Not Regular Hours Proof — 
> pre-market period. That means I have to base everything on different numbers. — Source GPS: y67l86cSqb8 | [MIDDLE-END] | CVD Strategy — Context: Proof thresholds from regular hours do not apply to pre-market. — 5.7 Correlation Alone Is Not Proof — 
> So I get a global overview of all these things, what's going on and that helps me a lot to give my position more confidence. — Source GPS: n7ZSkjb7JXs | [MIDDLE] | $3,400 pre-market trade — Context: Multi-asset correlation builds confidence but is not a standalone entry trigger. — END SECTION 5 — Section 6: Proof Timing — This section addresses WHEN to look for proof relative to price reaching the zone. — 6.1 Wait for Pullback vs Enter at Zone — Tom uses both approaches depending on context: — Wait for pullback: — 
> if, for example, I get a short pullback now and the market returns to acceptance and continues to trade high volumes, well, what is the logical conclusion? That we will most likely see a continuation of the trend. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — Context: For trend-continuation, Tom waits for the pullback to the zone, then looks for proof (acceptance + volume). — Enter at zone with limit order: — 
> For me, that means a great opportunity to place a limit order here, and then initially enter a short trade accordingly. — Source GPS: oa8kxSLLkAo | [MIDDLE] | Footprint tutorial — Context: For counter-trade at a predefined resistance with finished auction, Tom places a limit order at the zone. — 6.2 Proof Before Entry vs Proof After Entry — Tom's live trades show that proof can be observed: — Before entry: No liquidity at extreme, finished auction, B profile (structural proof visible before price reaches zone) — At entry: Absorption, aggressive buyers/sellers, market speed (observed at the moment of entry) — After entry: Delta decreasing, market slows down, rotation (observed after entry, used for management) — 6.3 Time-Based Proof Triggers — Tom uses time-based closes as proof triggers: — 
> we absolutely need to get a closing price now. then I'll keep the position. Otherwise, I'd just close out one contract right away — Source GPS: 4MoNjEQ2Dd8 | [MIDDLE] | $2,350 in 40 Minutes — 
> I see here that the last time there was significant trading volume on the 5-minut chart was at 603. And if it drops below that, things will break down — Source GPS: 4MoNjEQ2Dd8 | [END] | $2,350 in 40 Minutes — Context: 1-minute, 5-minute, and 15-minute closes are used as binary proof triggers (hold/exit). — END SECTION 6 — Section 7: Gaps — What Tom mentions but does not define, quantify, or systematize. — | # | Gap | Impact | Notes | |
